<title>UK: German inland gas oil declines, demand steadier.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil declines, demand steadier.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.5223)   DM/100 LTRS     DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     37.20/37.50     24.43/24.63     37.20/37.50</p>
<p> BREMEN		37.20/37.50     24.43/24.63     37.20/37.50</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    37.20/37.50     24.43/24.63     37.70/38.00</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   38.00/38.30     24.96/25.15     38.30/38.60</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   38.30/38.60     25.15/25.35     38.40/38.70</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  39.00/39.30     25.61/25.81     39.40/39.70</p>
<p>German inland gas oil prices were unchanged to slightly easier on Wednesday. Demand was heavier, with some consumers apparently concluding that prices will not go any lower in the short-term. -- London newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
